  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which words mean add?",
      "a": "Altogether, in total, sum, plus and both together often mean add. Always check that the story is about joining things.",
      "asks": [
        "What are addition clue words?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Does how many more mean add?",
      "a": "Usually no. How many more asks for the difference between two amounts, so you take away. If Ama has 15 and Kwame has 9, Ama has 15 take away 9, which is 6 more.",
      "asks": [
        "Is how many more a subtraction?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Which words mean multiply?",
      "a": "Each, every, groups of, lots of and times often mean multiply, when you put equal groups together. 4 tables with 6 at each is 4 times 6.",
      "asks": [
        "What are multiplication clue words?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Which words mean divide?",
      "a": "Share, share equally, split and how many in each group often mean divide. 20 mangoes shared equally between 5 baskets is 20 divided by 5, which is 4.",
      "asks": [
        "What are division clue words?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Can clue words trick me?",
      "a": "Yes. Each can appear in multiply and divide stories, and more can mean add or take away. Clue words are only hints, so always picture what is happening.",
      "asks": [
        "Are clue words always right?"
      ]
    }
